<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/00473bb2888b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In some TikTok videos, AI audio detectors reveal that the soundtracks have been manipulated." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4456" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/05a454a45f77> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "AI fakes, cyberattacks threaten German election" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4455" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/088faa66302e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "How are web platforms protecting the German electorate from fake news?" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4452" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0a1ef3025771> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Alice Weidel, co-leader of the Alternative for Germany party, before a virtual talk with Elon Musk on his platform X, last month." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4447" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0ab439dd0896> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "\"We're now dealing with a dual front,\" said Sasha Havlicek, chief executive of the Institute for Strategic Dialogue, a nonprofit research organization that on Thursday released a report about the Russian disinformation campaign on X." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4447" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0bfa226050a3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "At the same time, new so-called generative AI programs allow parties and individuals to create posts --- from text to images and even video --- much faster than before." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4455" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0dae02015c95> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4457] Russian bots have driven a dramatic surge of disinformation on the social media platform X, the report reads, adding that at the center of the effort to influence German voters is Doppelgänger, a Kremlin-backed operation, according to the German Office of Foreign Affairs." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4457" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0e8e50e78f5d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The claims have appeared in fake news outlets and in videos that have been altered by artificial intelligence. They have been spread by an army of bot accounts on social media platforms like X, Facebook, Telegram and, in a new development, Bluesky." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4447" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2135c7aab9fb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A Russian influence operation known as \"Storm-1516\" has set up over 100 websites using artificial intelligence (AI) to spread disinformation and meddle in Germany's upcoming elections." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4448" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/27c35a8334eb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Last week, with barely a fortnight to go until the German federal election on 23 February, manipulated TikTok videos showing hundreds of thousands of people apparently marching for the far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD) went viral." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4452" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/28e21f9668e3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The fake was 1 of several identified by Clemson University's Media Forensics Hub." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4447" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2a36be5dbe3d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "CeMAS said it had tracked down hundreds of German-language posts on the social network site X over the past month, exhibiting what it said showed typical patterns of Russia's Doppelganger disinformation campaign against the West that German, U.S. and French authorities have previously denounced." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4453" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/32fbdbbb49e7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "His public support of the Alternative for Germany on X, the social media network he owns, has aligned with Russia's strategic objective to destabilize Western democracies and support for Ukraine." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4447" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/346ab4947470> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4453] A Russian disinformation campaign is seeking to boost the far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD), undermine mainstream German parties and sow worries about the economy ahead of the country's Feb. 23 election, German think-tank CeMAS has found, Reuters reports." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4453" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/42d98261f32a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "And yet \"in Germany, we see that the party that spreads by far the most AI-generated content is the AfD,\" Munoz said, referring to an analysis she conducted around the European elections, as well as regional elections in 2024." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4455" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4301a36dae8e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Disinformation wave on rise in Germany ahead of elections" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4457" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/433918dde6ac> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Calin Georgescu, an independent nationalist and Eurosceptic candidate won the election, but the result was annulled after the Constitutional Court saw evidence of Russian interference in the voting process, particularly on TikTok, provided by the country's intelligence services." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4452" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/48d03c29aac7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Disinformation Clouds German Federal Election 2025" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4459" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/51c0ce022d9f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The police later clarified via their own X post, explaining the photo was taken during a scheduled school visit to the police station, not indicative of some wider societal alarm." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4459" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/56559bac1bc2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4453] All of these claims have one thing in common: they are disinformation, use artificial intelligence and deepfakes, and appear on fake news sites." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4453" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6a79f1228f3e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Many target Germany's support for Ukraine, claiming Berlin is prioritizing Kyiv over its own citizens. One example, documented in the report, describes a fabricated corruption scandal involving Economy Minister Robert Habeck and an unnamed 'Ukrainian Culture Minister.'" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4454" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6c99b08e183a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Justice Ministry of Rhineland-Palatinate has confirmed approximately 1,900 inmates will be eligible to vote." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4459" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/71e47a0164a3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A Russian disinformation campaign is seeking to boost the far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD), undermine mainstream German parties and sow worries about the economy ahead of the country's Feb. 23 election." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4453" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/752f6322f1e6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Intelligence agencies across the EU and U.S. have previously tracked Doppelgänger's highly coordinated tactics." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4454" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7555cdae4821> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The AfD Mayen-Koblenz Facebook page shared footage of police accompanying children, misrepresenting it as evidence of increased police protection." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4459" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/77b43d85133c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In December Romania's presidential elections were canceled after security services warned Russia was mounting 'aggressive' hybrid attacks." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4454" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/77daf2cb2430> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Last month, South Africa-born billionaire Elon Musk made a surprise appearance at an AfD campaign event in the eastern German city of Halle, which 4,500 people attended." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4456" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7973226f1e22> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "German authorities have also warned in recent weeks that a disinformation campaign originating from Moscow could be trying to influence the outcome of the election campaign." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4452" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7ee57a797a41> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Kremlin hopes the outcome of the contest, called ahead of schedule after Chancellor Olaf Scholz's center-left coalition collapsed late last year, could erode support in Europe for Ukraine." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4447" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7f62a9e03cb4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Snap, which owns Snapchat -- an instant messaging app which is estimated to have some 15 million monthly active (mostly young) users in Germany -- said its team is reviewing and fact-checking every political ad." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4452" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/84f974c8acc9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "\"These are some of the clearest examples of deepfakes being used for disinformation that I've seen,\" said Darren L. Linvill, a director of the hub who notified Ms. Finch about the manipulated video." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4447" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/87e578d49310> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "AI-driven Russian disinformation campaign targets German elections" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4448" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8ae7c0401191> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "On Jan. 30, 1 of the sites uploaded a video claiming that Vice Chancellor Robert Habeck conspired with Ukraine to steal 50 paintings from a Berlin art gallery." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4447" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/923b06c2d4af> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "German fact-check organisation GADMO said that in the run-up to the German election, issues such as the country's support for Ukraine continues to be a recurring theme." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4452" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/92bbe5af3141> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "According to Corrective's research, they are part of the new Russian influence operation nicknamed \"Bura-1516,\" which has been interfering in the election campaign ahead of the federal elections for three months." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4453" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/963e765178ab> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Rumors have surfaced concerning President Frank-Walter Steinmeier allegedly saying the election could be annulled should right-wing parties win." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4459" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9bd2e8e84e9b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The network mimics real German news outlets and promotes nationalist and Eurosceptic narratives, particularly supporting the Alternative für Deutschland (AfD) party while targeting mainstream politicians." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4448" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a20cde58d512> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Doppelgänger-linked websites have previously cloned outlets like Der Spiegel, altering domain names just slightly to deceive unsuspecting readers." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4457" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a4a25c6ee753> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Many, like Naomi Seibt, a 24-year-old vaccine and climate change skeptic, now post content in English to attract his attention." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4447" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a4e42de5d326> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The campaign uses fake news sites, sleeper accounts, and AI-generated content to spread false narratives and erode trust in Western institutions." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4457" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a807e8f7b2ff> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google's YouTube said its recommender system will highlight relevant news sources." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4452" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a8a0acfde36e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Similarly, the AfD’s use of AI-generated campaign videos has drawn scrutiny." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4459" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/af688c693b2a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "1 such video depicted Health Minister Karl Lauterbach being forcibly removed by police, which Lauterbach condemned, stating, “Such videos, AI fakes, stoke hatred in our society.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4459" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b0114604fd4e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In Germany, Russia is employing tactics it has honed in France, Moldova, Georgia, the United States and other countries that have recently held elections, according to disinformation researchers including from the Institute for Strategic Dialogue, CeMAS and Recorded Future, a threat intelligence company based in Massachusetts." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4447" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b2e6fb566de6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4452] The European Commission last month asked Microsoft, TikTok, LinkedIn, Google, Snap, Meta and X to take part in a stress test, to make sure they have appropriate risk mitigation measures in place." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4452" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b82acb3a0bbe> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Russian bots have driven a dramatic surge of disinformation on the social media platform X days before Germany's election, according to a government report seen by POLITICO." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4454" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/be94fb9d8a20> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Czech and Belgian authorities busted a major influence network they said was spreading pro-Kremlin propaganda in the runup to last year's European Parliament vote." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4454" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c40d2901fe63> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The network was identified by a joint investigation of Correctiv and NewsGuard, which found that the campaign has fabricated false claims about German politicians, including deepfake videos and misleading reports, to manipulate public perception." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4448" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c951e991599a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Originating from the Prigozhin-linked Russian Foundation to Battle Injustice (R-FBI), this absurd claim was amplified through a network of Russian-aligned websites, including inauthentic news outlets and social media accounts, reaching hundreds of thousands of users across platforms such as Threads, Telegram, and X, writes Euvsdisinfo." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4453" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cba1e0192f6d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4452] The European Commission last month asked Microsoft, TikTok, LinkedIn, Google, Snap, Meta and X to take part in a stress test, to make sure they have appropriate risk mitigation measures in place." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4452" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cc6fef39164c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Putin’s bot army tries to swing German election" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4454" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cd2413b123d2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tens of thousands of people in Germany did take to the streets last weekend --- but to protest the leader of the centre-right Christian Democratic Union (CDU) Friedrich Merz and his parliamentary proposal on stricter migration rules." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4456" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ce492fbed6b8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Mr. Musk's posts on X have been spread by bot accounts operated by a Russian influence operation known as Doppelgänger, according to CeMAS, an organization that tracks German online extremism." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4447" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cf711a2db50e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In January, Mr. Musk interviewed the party's leading candidate, Alice Weidel, for 75 minutes on X, the same platform he gave Donald J. Trump during his run for office last August." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4447" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d99b03260f4d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In October 2023 he shared a meme created as part of an influence campaign run by Social Design Agency, an internet company in Moscow that has been sanctioned by the United States." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4447" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/dd7fd3269cf9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Kremlin wants to influence German elections through disinformation" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4453" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ec939d50a1dd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Meta's Facebook and Instagram became the subject of a European Commission investigation over how the platforms tackle disinformation under the Digital Services Act (DSA)." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4452" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f426d41bc9d0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Between Russia and Elon Musk, German Voters Face a ‘Dual Front’ of Disinformation" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4447" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f5adb994dcec> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "German officials identified more than 100 pseudo-news websites quietly accumulating content for months, according to officials." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4454" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/fdafdacb3ce5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Euroverify ran the videos through a series of AI image detectors." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4456" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/fe1498a5e52f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Fake TikTok videos show hundreds of thousands marching for AfD in Germany" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4456" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ffe1c2670ffc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4452] Meta's Facebook and Instagram became the subject of a European Commission investigation over how the platforms tackle disinformation under the Digital Services Act (DSA)." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4452" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/Risk/7254aca29c24> a airo:Risk ;
    rdfs:label "Risk of AI-generated disinformation influencing elections and undermining democratic processes" ;
    airo:confidenceScore "0.9"^^xsd:float ;
